# Lets GitHub show "Cite this repository". Keep title, version, abstract,
# keywords, url and licence in step with package.json: `npm run metadata`
# checks them, and the test suite runs that check.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use or refer to Fell Runner, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: Fell Runner
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-10-18
abstract: A speedrunning platformer, inspired by Celeste, over three notorious Lake District fells, with real routes, seeded weather, wind physics, ghosts and full accessibility. Free to play in your browser.
authors:
  - given-names: Ryan
    family-names: McCrickerd
repository-code: https://github.com/rmcrkd/fell-runner
url: https://rmcrkd.github.io/fell-runner/
license: MIT
keywords:
  - game
  - browser-game
  - platformer
  - speedrun
  - celeste-like
  - pixel-art
  - html5-canvas
  - javascript
  - accessibility
  - a11y
  - lake-district
  - fell-running
  - seeded-random
  - github-pages
  - zero-dependencies
